Z||000000||Ironhorse||04-27-2000||12:43 AM||||I'm ready to drop my 2.8 in 85 GT..  I'm gonna clean every bracket, bolts, clean the cradle, block, oil pan, the head, Platium (sp) forgive me still learning fiero stuff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, manifold, valve cover, and whatever else need serious cleaning.  And gonna repaint every one with proper paint. for Platium gonna powder coat along with exhaust manifold.  Here is the thing.. If I take it to shop will they acid dip it or is there something that I can make in a old bathtub to acid dip it myself, I heard about something called mineral cleaning product but i want something stong that It can bathe overnite or soemething, this thing got 15 years of gunk, sh*t, and stuff that sciencist can't indentify.  Any help would be appreaciated. (BTW, sue me for lousy spelling  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )||||reg||10
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||04-27-2000||01:38 AM||||The Plenum will probably be bead blasted by the powdercoater before he does anything else to it. I had a Honda Three-wheeler frame and all brakets, etc. powder-coated a few years ago and the guy did all the prep.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BigBoyToys||04-27-2000||07:48 PM||||Hey, Check out this link for infor on a bathtub type approach to cleaning metal (steel) parts such as manifolds. But be careful and read all the instructions and do test pieces first. This can actually eat entire part if left to long. Hope this works because I have not yet posted a url.<BR> <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/_XMCM/nlindsey/restoration/Electrolysis/Electrolysis.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/_XMCM/nlindsey/restoration/Electrolysis/Electrolysis.htm</A> <BR>BBT||||reg||3
Z||000003||Ironhorse||04-27-2000||09:06 PM||||uhh BigBoy Toy, umm heh... I don't think I'm gonna risk my parts I might happen to leave it in there for a couple of min longer and only to find puddle of steel. I thought manifold parts is alumium, not steel?  Oh well.. I'm gonna look into this product muriatic acid or a sub for muriatic acid.. gonna do some research before deciding||||reg||1
Z||000004||Master_Sushi||04-27-2000||09:13 PM||||would a powersprayer work? Im sure it would at least help some.||||reg||12
Z||000006||Gokart||04-27-2000||09:53 PM||||Soaked some bolts and exhaust parts in muriatic acid in a thick metal pan a couple of weeks ago and it ate right through the pan in about 10 minutes! There was no directions on the bottle except for pool cleaning so I didn't dilute it. Probably should have <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> That stuff is EVIL!||||reg||2
Z||000007||Ironhorse||04-27-2000||10:04 PM||||Gokart. That's the stuff I'm looking for (EVIL GRIN), Where did you get yours at.  Ya know I would do this if I were you, I would get a pan, bucket or whatever that is the same material that the canister is holding that acid.. if it's plastic, get a plastic bucket or whatever.  I would not just dip it in and bath it over nite.. I would put it in for about 10 second, rinse it off with water, then dip it again for 10 sec, rinse it off, I would say total of 2 or 3 time... from the sound of it, it don't take long to clean the GUNK, SH*T, AND WHATEVER ELSE is in there.  Let me know where you get your and I'll do a trial on some other metal stuff before I let any of my Fiero parts touch it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Gokart||04-27-2000||10:22 PM||||Right at True Value hardware! I bet any hardware store would have it. Yah, that's what I did when I soaked them a 2nd time. I cut the empty bottle at the top and poured the stuff from the new bottle into it. Soaked them right away after cause it leaves the rust film if you don't. STAND BACK when pouring! I got a whiff of this stuff and it about knocked me on my ass! Maybe that's what's wrong with me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||2
